---
/**
 * 영어 개인정보처리방침 (/en/privacy/). 한국어 방침(src/pages/privacy.astro)과 같은 내용이다.
 * 한국어판을 고치면 이 페이지와 시행일도 함께 고친다.
 */
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { contactEmail, siteConfig } from '../../site.config';

/** 한국어판과 같은 날로 둔다 */
const effectiveDate = 'October 15, 2026';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`What information ${siteConfig.name} collects and how it is handled. Your files are never collected.`}
  note={`Effective: ${effectiveDate}`}
>
  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not collect the files you use in the tools. Your files never leave your device.</li>
    <li>There is no sign-up, so we never ask for your name, phone number or similar details.</li>
    <li>Cookies are used only for ads.</li>
    <li>
      Apart from emails you send us, we only collect visit statistics, which cannot tell us who you
      are.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your files</h2>
  <p>
    Files you use in the tools are processed only inside your browser on your device. File content
    and file names are never sent anywhere, including to this site's servers, and we cannot see
    them. When you close the page, any file data left in the browser is gone too.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Visit statistics</h3>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see how much each page is used. It does not use cookies and
    does not identify or track individual visitors. It collects:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The address of the page you visited and the page you came from (referrer)</li>
    <li>Your browser and operating system type, and the country you visited from</li>
    <li>How long the page took to load</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The analytics script runs only outside the tool area. The tool area is an isolated space, so the
    script cannot read your file content or file names.
  </p>

  <h3>Access logs</h3>
  <p>
    This site is served through Cloudflare's servers. Cloudflare processes access logs containing
    information such as IP addresses to deliver the site and block attacks. We do not use these logs
    to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h3>Emails you send us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and the content of your message. We use them only
    to reply, keep them for one year after we finish replying, and then delete them. If you ask us
    to delete them sooner, we will do so right away.
  </p>

  <h2>Ads and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site is funded by Google AdSense ads. When you open a page, Google's ad script is loaded,
    and Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on your visits to this and other
    sites.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can turn off personalized ads in{' '}
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">
        Google Ad Settings
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>
      See{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
        how Google uses information
      </a>{' '}
      from sites that use its services.
    </li>
    <li>You can delete or block stored cookies in your browser settings.</li>
    <li>
      In regions where consent is required, such as Europe, you can choose whether to allow cookies
      in Google's consent message.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Ads only appear outside the tool area. The tool area is an isolated space, so ads cannot read
    your file content or file names.
  </p>
  {siteConfig.ads.enabled && siteConfig.ads.adblockNotice && (
    <p>
      If an ad blocker is on, a message asks you to turn it off. We only check on your device
      whether the ads could be loaded, and the result is never sent anywhere.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>What we store in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The only things this site stores itself are your light or dark theme choice, the language you
    picked, and data you chose to download in the tools.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Public files the tools use, such as fonts, are kept in this browser's storage only when you
      click "Download", so you do not have to download them again next time.
    </li>
    <li>
      We also note which data you chose to download, so we can tell you when a kept copy has been
      removed and needs to be downloaded again.
    </li>
    <li>
      None of this includes the files you use in the tools or their names, and it is never sent to a
      server. Clearing this site's data in your browser settings removes all of it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information. The following services process information as described in this
    policy to help us run the site.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cloudflare (USA): serving the site, visit statistics, forwarding contact emails</li>
    <li>Google (USA): storing contact emails (Gmail), ads (AdSense)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These companies are based outside Korea, so this information may be transferred to and processed
    in other countries, including the USA.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see or delete the emails you sent us. Contact us at the address below and we will
    take care of it. Visit statistics cannot be linked to any person, so we cannot find or delete
    them for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If the way we handle information changes, for example by adding an analytics tool or ad
    provider, we will update this page and its effective date before the change.
  </p>

  <h2>Language</h2>
  <p>
    This English version is a translation. If it differs from the
    <a href="/privacy/">Korean version</a>, the Korean version prevails.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.name} (site operator)
    <br />
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
  </p>
</DocLayout>
